    <briefdescription>
<para>Which file each drawn component&apos;s remapped section goes in <ndash/> see <ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1af50bcf7fc1329c1c3fe0980e4060b036" kindref="member">fileGroups</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
THE MOD&apos;S OWN TEXTURE LINES, RE-KEYED BY ROLE. Each ``&lt;texRegPrefix&gt;N`` line of the mod&apos;s sections, for each
drawn component of the plan, goes to the register that component&apos;s bindings read its texture&apos;s role at
(:cpp:func:`registerOf`) -- the layout of the fix&apos;s own list, which the lines sit after. The role is the
parser&apos;s (:cpp:func:`IniParseData::roleOfResource`: one it chose the file for among the roles a drawn component
binds, this component&apos;s first, or the one it refused the file for).

- With :cpp:member:`carryByRegisterRole`, a texture put into another KIND of slot on purpose goes by the slot:
  to the register for the role the source reads there, its file unchanged -- or is left alone.
- A line whose role or register is unknown is left alone, unless the component&apos;s ``&quot;main&quot;`` list binds that
  register: then it is dropped -- except a file of no known role where the source reads the same kind as the
  target.
- A file the parser refused for its role does not go back: the line binds what the role resolved to, or is
  dropped where nothing stands in -- except on a component its own shader draws, which keeps the mod&apos;s art.

A line left alone is not listed
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parser&apos;s data of the mod&apos;s <computeroutput>.ini</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>roles</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>What the roles resolve to (<ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1a0e426d1d6de387f34992a769db6f1a2a" kindref="member">roleResources</ref>), with a reroute&apos;s entries copied from its source component </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lists</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The texture lists (<ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1ac459cc6f5d3c25dd7ddf40209d292c45" kindref="member">textureLists</ref>, <ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1a9e3d02a6d63ce36f2d6adefb5c0632ea" kindref="member">toggleLists</ref>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>drawn</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The source components the mod draws, reroutes included </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rerouteFrom</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A reroute that took draws -&gt; the component it took them from </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ownShader</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The drawn components their own :cpp:member:<computeroutput><ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_source_component_1aa1b6a7a373ca8fc31230b53c3c057f7a" kindref="member">SourceComponent::shader</ref></computeroutput> draws</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Source component -&gt; its lines the fix moves or drops, in the order the mod first writes them </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
